{"value": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/pulls/6473", "id": 2880406671, "node_id": "PR_kwDOABUVKc6rr4SP", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-kie/pull/6473", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-kie/pull/6473.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-kie/pull/6473.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/issues/6473", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/pulls/6473/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/pulls/6473/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/issues/6473/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/statuses/4a8499788600e1a865e01062ced9c16023e8a0ec", "number": 6473, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "[incubator-kie-issues-6472] Make exec\u2011model consequence argument order deterministic", "user": {"login": "hwu2024", "id": 113719534, "node_id": "U_kgDOBsc47g", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113719534?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024", "html_url": "https://github.com/hwu2024", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hwu2024/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "<!--\r\n  Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one\r\n  or more contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file\r\n  distributed with this work for additional information\r\n  regarding copyright ownership.  The ASF licenses this file\r\n  to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the\r\n  \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance\r\n  with the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\r\n\r\n    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\r\n\r\n  Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing,\r\n  software distributed under the License is distributed on an\r\n  \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY\r\n  KIND, either express or implied.  See the License for the\r\n  specific language governing permissions and limitations\r\n  under the License.\r\n  -->\r\n\r\n**Thank you for submitting this pull request**\r\n\r\n**NOTE!:** Double-check the target branch for this PR.\r\nThe default is `main` so it will target Drools 8 / Kogito.\r\n\r\n**Ports** If a forward-port or a backport is needed, paste the forward port PR here\r\n\r\n* N/A\r\n\r\n**Issue**: _(please edit the GitHub Issues link if it exists)_\r\n\r\n* [Link](https://github.com/apache/incubator-kie-drools/issues/6472)\r\n\r\n**referenced Pull Requests**: _(please edit the URLs of referenced pullrequests if they exist)_\r\n\r\n* N/A\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n**Modules:** `drools-model/drools-model-codegen`  \r\n**Area:** Exec\u2011model consequence generation (`D.on(...)` & `LambdaConsequence\u2026`)\r\n\r\nThis PR makes exec\u2011model consequence argument order deterministic so the list passed to `D.on(...)` always matches the parameter order of the generated `LambdaConsequence\u2026` (i.e., the `BlockN<\u2026>` functional type). The change prevents compile\u2011time mismatches that sometimes occurred in generated sources when iteration order differs across environments.\r\n\r\n## Root cause\r\n\r\n* Unordered iteration of a `Set` (e.g., from `Collectors.toSet()`) when determining the argument list for `D.on(...)` and the parameter list for the corresponding lambda.  \r\n* Because the two lists are computed from a container with unspecified iteration order, the two orders can differ\u2014leading to compile\u2011time errors like:\r\n```\r\nThe method execute(Block2<String,List<String>>) in the type ConsequenceBuilder._2<String,List<String>>\r\nis not applicable for the arguments (LambdaConsequence\u2026)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Related Tests\r\n\r\n`TypeCoercionTest#testComparisonCoercion` \r\n`TypeCoercionTest#testComparisonCoercion2` \r\n`TypeCoercionTest#testFloatOperation` \r\n`TypeCoercionTest#testPrimitiveCoercion` \r\n`TypeObjectCoercionTest#testCoercionStringVsExplicitIntegerWithMap` \r\n`RuleAttributesTest#testDynamicSalience`\r\n\r\n## Fixes\r\n\r\n1) Preserve encounter order when collecting used declarations, and reuse that single ordered sequence in both places:\r\n   * Replace unordered `toSet()` collectors with `toCollection(LinkedHashSet::new)` (or collect to a `List`), ensuring a stable encounter order.  \r\n   * Thread the same ordered sequence through the construction of `D.on(...)` and the `LambdaConsequence\u2026` parameter boxing.\r\n\r\n2) Define ordering policy:\r\n   * Java dialect (AST): order by first appearance in `ruleConsequence.findAll(NameExpr)` (reading order).\r\n   * MVEL dialect (string): order by first index of occurrence in the consequence string.\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>\r\nHow to replicate CI configuration locally?\r\n</summary>\r\n\r\nBuild Chain tool does \"simple\" maven build(s), the builds are just Maven commands, but because the repositories relates and depends on each other and any change in API or class method could affect several of those repositories there is a need to use [build-chain tool](https://github.com/kiegroup/github-action-build-chain) to handle cross repository builds and be sure that we always use latest version of the code for each repository.\r\n \r\n[build-chain tool](https://github.com/kiegroup/github-action-build-chain) is a build tool which can be used on command line locally or in Github Actions workflow(s), in case you need to change multiple repositories and send multiple dependent pull requests related with a change you can easily reproduce the same build by executing it on Github hosted environment or locally in your development environment. See [local execution](https://github.com/kiegroup/github-action-build-chain#local-execution) details to get more information about it.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>\r\nHow to retest this PR or trigger a specific build:\r\n</summary>\r\n\r\n- for <b>pull request and downstream checks</b>  \r\n  - Push a new commit to the PR. An empty commit would be enough.\r\n\r\n- for a <b>full downstream build</b>\r\n  - for <b>github actions</b> job: add the label `run_fdb`\r\n\r\n- for <b>Jenkins PR check only</b>\r\n  - If you are an ASF committer for KIE podling, login to Jenkins (https://ci-builds.apache.org/job/KIE/job/drools/), go to the specific PR job, and click on `Build Now` button.\r\n</details>\r\n", "labels": [{"id": 9394570633, "node_id": "LA_kwDOABUVKc8AAAACL_XFiQ", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-kie/labels/area:rules", "name": "area:rules", "description": "", "color": "fbca04", "default": false, "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}], "milestone": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "created_at": "2025-10-02T04:41:35Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-08T07:19:10Z", "closed_at": "2025-10-08T07:19:10Z", "merged_at": "2025-10-08T07:19:10Z", "merge_commit_sha": "ac50f75c39b97d46e109f96e7bd6e11f44feae32", "assignee": null, "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "head": {"label": "hwu2024:incubator-kie-issues-6472", "ref": "incubator-kie-issues-6472", "repo": {"id": 1068195103, "node_id": "R_kgDOP6tdHw", "name": "incubator-kie-drools", "full_name": "hw